    "['mpls lsr-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls interface lo0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols mpls interface lo0.0\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-interface 2.2.2.9\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the MPLS LSR-ID is typically configured by:\\n1. Ensuring the loopback interface (lo0.0) is included in MPLS protocols\\n2. The router automatically uses the loopback's IP address as the LSR-ID\\n3. If explicitly needed, you can use `label-switched-interface` to specify the LSR-ID\\n\\nThe equivalent of Huawei's `mpls lsr-id 2.2.2.9` is primarily achieved by configuring the loopback interface under MPLS protocols in Juniper.\", 'trans_template': None}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-interface 2.2.2.9', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-interface 2.2.2.9', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols mpls interface lo0.0\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-interface 2.2.2.9\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the MPLS LSR-ID is typically configured by:\\n1. Ensuring the loopback interface (lo0.0) is included in MPLS protocols\\n2. The router automatically uses the loopback's IP address as the LSR-ID\\n3. If explicitly needed, you can use `label-switched-interface` to specify the LSR-ID\\n\\nThe equivalent of Huawei's `mpls lsr-id 2.2.2.9` is primarily achieved by configuring the loopback interface under MPLS protocols in Juniper.\", 'trans_template': None}]]": 1,
    "['mpls', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols mpls interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want to enable MPLS on specific interfaces (similar to the Huawei config where it's enabled on GE1/0/1 and GE1/0/3), it would be:\\n##\\nset protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/1\\nset protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/3\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on whether you want to enable MPLS globally (first example) or on specific interfaces (second example). The Huawei `mpls` command in interface context enables MPLS on that particular interface.\", 'trans_template': None}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols mpls interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want to enable MPLS on specific interfaces (similar to the Huawei config where it's enabled on GE1/0/1 and GE1/0/3), it would be:\\n##\\nset protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/1\\nset protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/3\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on whether you want to enable MPLS globally (first example) or on specific interfaces (second example). The Huawei `mpls` command in interface context enables MPLS on that particular interface.\", 'trans_template': None}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/3', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols mpls interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want to enable MPLS on specific interfaces (similar to the Huawei config where it's enabled on GE1/0/1 and GE1/0/3), it would be:\\n##\\nset protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/1\\nset protocols mpls interface ge-1/0/3\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on whether you want to enable MPLS globally (first example) or on specific interfaces (second example). The Huawei `mpls` command in interface context enables MPLS on that particular interface.\", 'trans_template': None}]]": 1,
    "['mpls ldp', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ldp interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want to be more specific about the interfaces (similar to the Huawei config where LDP is enabled per interface), you could use:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/3.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on whether you want to enable LDP globally on all interfaces (first example) or selectively on specific interfaces (second example), matching the Huawei configuration's approach.\", 'trans_template': None}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want to be more specific about the interfaces (similar to the Huawei config where LDP is enabled per interface), you could use:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/3.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on whether you want to enable LDP globally on all interfaces (first example) or selectively on specific interfaces (second example), matching the Huawei configuration's approach.\", 'trans_template': None}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/3.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/3.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you want to be more specific about the interfaces (similar to the Huawei config where LDP is enabled per interface), you could use:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/1.0\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-1/0/3.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on whether you want to e